  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\operatorname{ar}^{\\mathrm{n}}=57 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{ar}+\\mathrm{ar}^2+\\infty=57 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{1-\\mathrm{r}}=57 \\ldots(I)\\\\\n& \\sum_{\\mathrm{n}=0}^{\\infty} \\mathrm{a}^3 \\mathrm{r}^{3 \\mathrm{n}}=9747 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{a}^3+\\mathrm{a}^3 \\cdot \\mathrm{r}^3+\\mathrm{a}^3 \\cdot \\mathrm{r}^6+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots . \\ldots=9746 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{a}^3}{1-\\mathrm{r}^3}=9746 \\ldots(II)\\\\\n& \\frac{(\\mathrm{I})^3}{(\\mathrm{II})} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\frac{\\mathrm{a}^3}{(1-\\mathrm{r})^3}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{a}^3}{1-\\mathrm{r}^3}}=\\frac{57^3}{9717}=19 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{a}=19 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{a}+18 \\mathrm{r}=19+18 \\times \\frac{2}{3}=31 \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}$<br />On solving, $\\mathrm{r}=\\frac{2}{3}$ and $\\mathrm{r}=\\frac{3}{2}$ (rejected $)$\n$\\begin{aligned} & a=19 \\\\ & \\therefore a+18 r=19+18 \\times \\frac{2}{3}=31\\end{aligned}$",
